WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(audience applauding)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:03.090
- Well, your son recently
graduated from USC.

00:00:03.090 --> 00:00:03.930
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:05.450
Was that crazy for you?

00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:06.283
Were you,
- That was crazy.

00:00:06.283 --> 00:00:07.116
(audience sympathizing)
- were you just a mess?

00:00:07.116 --> 00:00:07.949
- Well.
(Lisa laughing)

00:00:07.949 --> 00:00:08.782
Oh yeah.

00:00:08.782 --> 00:00:10.380
- I mean, I have a five year old boy,

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:12.720
and I'm just like, this moment, like,

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:13.799
- Oh yeah.

00:00:13.799 --> 00:00:14.632
do you think back when he was
(Lisa exclaiming)

00:00:14.632 --> 00:00:15.750
five and you're just like,

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:17.220
he's so, he's a man.

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:19.380
- I did then, but I'm telling you,

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:21.690
leading up to his graduation, I was like,

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:23.880
'cause my own graduation from college,

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:26.310
I was like, "That's just a
ceremony" and "Who cares?"

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:28.770
And, "Oh my God, do we
really have to get up early?

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:32.100
What? Uh, we've been up
all night celebrating."

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:34.080
So, when I heard that his was like,

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:35.527
really early in the morning and I said,

00:00:35.527 --> 00:00:38.490
"So, are any of you going?"
(Lisa and Kelly laughing)

00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:40.027
And he said,

00:00:40.027 --> 00:00:42.586
"Yeah, we're all going".

00:00:42.586 --> 00:00:43.419
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:00:43.419 --> 00:00:44.252
- Weird question.

00:00:44.252 --> 00:00:45.270
- Like, "What's wrong with you?"

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:46.770
And I said, "Oh, well, no, of course.

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:48.919
And I'm gonna be there too, yeah."

00:00:48.919 --> 00:00:49.752
(audience laughing)

00:00:49.752 --> 00:00:50.585
- So excited.

00:00:50.585 --> 00:00:52.481
- I was like, "Wow, they
really care. That's great."

00:00:52.481 --> 00:00:53.386
(Kelly laughing)

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:54.690
And then I get there and I'm a wreck.

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:55.860
I'm taking pictures.

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:57.540
I'm getting the pictures of the moment

00:00:57.540 --> 00:00:58.980
they call his name, and you know,

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:00.365
- Yeah.

00:01:00.365 --> 00:01:02.370
just, I was, I went nuts,

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:05.640
and it stayed with me
for a week afterward.

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:07.110
I can't believe how dumb I am.

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:08.340
And I was like, "Well, I mean,

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:09.900
you're not gonna care. Are you?"

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:11.194
- Oh my God,

00:01:11.194 --> 00:01:12.027
- What?
I will be the one weeping,

00:01:12.027 --> 00:01:12.860
and pictures,
- Yeah.

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:14.265
- and embarrassing my children.

00:01:14.265 --> 00:01:15.347
- And I was. And then look,
- Yeah.

00:01:15.347 --> 00:01:17.267
- it was like, "I love you so much.

00:01:17.267 --> 00:01:18.960
I can't believe you graduated.

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:20.886
I'm so happy."
(both laughing)

00:01:20.886 --> 00:01:21.840
- Oh, that's so awesome. I love that.

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:23.760
Wait, I think that Courtney Cox said

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:25.980
at one point that you're very competitive.

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:27.840
- Oh, well.
- I'm very competitive.

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:28.770
Is this true?

00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:29.940
- Yeah.
- I am too.

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:32.280
- But intense.
- Very intense.

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:34.170
- I mean it's, I think there's a fine line

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:36.180
between intense and competitive.

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:37.560
- That's what people say to me as well,

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:39.300
but somehow the line gets blurred.

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:40.133
- It gets blurred.
(audience laughing)

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:40.966
Yeah, I guess.

00:01:40.966 --> 00:01:42.750
I mean, it's not like I'll,

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:43.583
I'll be mean,

00:01:43.583 --> 00:01:45.519
or try to sabotage anyone.
- No, no.

00:01:45.519 --> 00:01:46.893
- I really, I would never
- No, I don't wanna cheat.

00:01:46.893 --> 00:01:47.726
- No.
- No.

00:01:47.726 --> 00:01:48.559
- Cheating?

00:01:48.559 --> 00:01:49.736
- I can't stand people that-
- That's not a win.

00:01:49.736 --> 00:01:50.569
- No, it's not a win.
- It's not a win.

00:01:50.569 --> 00:01:51.721
- Doesn't count.

00:01:51.721 --> 00:01:52.554
(Kelly gasping)

00:01:52.554 --> 00:01:54.000
We oughta play a game next time.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:54.833
- Yeah, how about it.
- Okay okay,

00:01:54.833 --> 00:01:55.800
'cause I love games.

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:56.633
Okay. Okay.
- Yeah.

00:01:56.633 --> 00:01:58.020
- Well the first trip that you took,

00:01:58.020 --> 00:01:59.367
um, as a cast was,
- Yeah,

00:01:59.367 --> 00:02:01.380
- um, was that, was that for Friends?

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:02.700
That was in Vegas?

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:03.960
- Yes.
- Y'all gambled?

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:05.040
- Well, yeah.
- Okay.

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:06.990
- I mean to me, we went
to Vegas to gamble.

00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:07.950
I think to everyone else,

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:10.770
we went to connect, but um.
(Kelly laughing)

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:12.520
'cause I get, intense.
- You were like blank check.

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:14.760
- Yeah. Intense, about gambling.

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:16.207
It's like, "Well we're gonna go eat."

00:02:16.207 --> 00:02:19.860
"Eat? Why would you spend,
waste time eating when

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:22.110
I can still be playing and winning?"

00:02:22.110 --> 00:02:24.053
- Yeah.
- I love you.

00:02:24.053 --> 00:02:24.886
- Yeah.

00:02:24.886 --> 00:02:25.719
- Okay. You are very competitive.

00:02:25.719 --> 00:02:26.959
- Yeah.
- Was it a fun trip though?

00:02:26.959 --> 00:02:27.792
- Oh yeah.

00:02:27.792 --> 00:02:28.728
- 'Cause y'all didn't know at the time,

00:02:28.728 --> 00:02:29.561
- No, we didn't know.
- that it was gonna blow up.

00:02:29.561 --> 00:02:31.200
- No, we hadn't, we hadn't.

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:32.310
it hadn't been on the air yet,

00:02:32.310 --> 00:02:34.200
and Jim Burrows got Warner Brothers.

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:37.500
It was the most
unbelievably exciting thing

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.500
to give him the private jet.

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:41.932
- Yeah.

00:02:41.932 --> 00:02:42.765
- And take just the six of us,

00:02:42.765 --> 00:02:44.850
no boyfriends, spouses, or anything,

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:46.440
and go to Las Vegas.

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:48.630
And he took us to dinner at Spago.

00:02:48.630 --> 00:02:49.973
- Wow.
- And he said,

00:02:49.973 --> 00:02:52.110
- Fancy.
- "You need to be aware,

00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:54.060
that at this moment, right now,

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:55.920
the six of you are together at dinner,

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:57.150
after this show airs,

00:02:57.150 --> 00:02:59.619
you won't be able to do this anymore."

00:02:59.619 --> 00:03:00.452
(audience exclaiming)

00:03:00.452 --> 00:03:01.285
- Oh, he knew.

00:03:01.285 --> 00:03:02.118
- I guess he did.
- Yeah.

00:03:02.118 --> 00:03:04.260
- And everyone else was like, "Wow."

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:07.308
And I thought, "Well, who knows? I mean."

00:03:07.308 --> 00:03:09.269
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:03:09.269 --> 00:03:10.410
- I mean, it's a toss up.
- I know.

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:13.184
Look at me. What does Jim Burrows know?

00:03:13.184 --> 00:03:14.730
(Kelly clapping)
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:03:14.730 --> 00:03:16.683
I've always been fun like that.

00:03:17.610 --> 00:03:19.470
- Wait, that was me on
American Idol though.

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:21.360
Everybody was like, "This
show's gonna be all like."

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:22.230
They gave us money.

00:03:22.230 --> 00:03:23.790
They dropped us off at a mall,

00:03:23.790 --> 00:03:27.030
and they gave us money
to like, buy clothes,

00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:28.080
to wear on television.

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:30.007
And I was like,
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:30.007 --> 00:03:32.314
"I got bills to pay."
(Lisa and audience laughing)

00:03:32.314 --> 00:03:33.930
I was like, I like, wore my own clothes.

00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:36.180
I was like, "This show's going nowhere."

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:37.830
I'm just like, "Hopefully I can get a job

00:03:37.830 --> 00:03:39.240
somehow singing somewhere."

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:40.230
I was the same way.

00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:41.190
I think when you think like that,

00:03:41.190 --> 00:03:42.540
it's better though. You don't,

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:43.373
you know, you don't.
- Yeah, Yeah.

00:03:43.373 --> 00:03:44.562
- Your expectations

00:03:44.562 --> 00:03:45.687
are managed.
- Keep them low.

00:03:45.687 --> 00:03:46.520
- Yeah. They are.
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:47.353
- Keep them low.

